WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.790
- [Narrator] This Great
Big Story was made possible

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:03.200
by Wells Fargo.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:07.068
Established 1852, re-established 2018.

00:00:07.068 --> 00:00:07.901
(jaunty music)

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:09.910
This is Myron.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:10.900
- Hi.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.840
- [Narrator] Myron is an athlete.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.650
- I played a little football in college.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:15.680
- [Narrator] And ...

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.030
- I was a Rhodes Scholar.

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:18.060
- [Narrator] And ...

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.526
- I played for the NFL.

00:00:19.526 --> 00:00:20.660
- [Narrator] And ...

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.368
- I have a Master's degree
in Medical Anthropology.

00:00:23.368 --> 00:00:24.640
- [Narrator] And ...

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.010
- And, I'm a neurosurgeon.

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:27.010
- [Narrator] Sheesh.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.400
- My first dream

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.380
was to play professional football.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:37.620
There's no question.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.540
I was very active as a
young man, and I knew

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.480
that I was pretty good at it.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.300
When I got to the fifth
grade, that's when I knew

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.460
I wanted to pursue my second dream.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:49.140
I read a book called
Gifted Hands by Ben Carson,

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.450
who looked like me-he was black-

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:53.910
who came from a similar
socioeconomic background as me.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:55.690
We didn't have much money
when we left the Bahamas

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:58.060
and came to America, and
the more I read about it

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:00.700
the more I knew that once I
was done playing football,

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:02.280
neurosurgery was gonna be the pathway

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:03.980
and the second chapter of my life.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:06.480
I was the number one-rated
high school player

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:09.110
in the country for
football-recruited by everyone-

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:10.500
83 scholarship offers.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:13.560
I always felt that football fed academics,

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.530
academics fed football.

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:17.500
- [Narrator] Myron spent his college years

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:20.440
playing football and shadowing doctors.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:22.480
He graduated in two and a half years

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:24.940
and was expected to be a first
or second round draft pick

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:27.800
in the NFL with a
multi-million dollar contract,

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:29.860
but he also had a chance to study

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:31.393
at Oxford as a Rhodes scholar.

00:01:32.262 --> 00:01:33.790
- I ended up deciding to go to Oxford

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:35.320
and saying no to the NFL.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:37.220
I spent a year and a half over there.

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:39.200
I came back to the United States,

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.910
went into the draft and got
drafted in the sixth round

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.540
instead of the second or first,

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:46.250
made $70,000 instead of six million.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.960
Played for three years, got out healthy,

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:50.870
felt good about my time there,

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:53.570
and, frankly, made enough money
to pay for medical school.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:55.390
I didn't have any lasting concussions,

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:56.770
and my hands were okay to where I was able

00:01:56.770 --> 00:01:58.410
to do surgery in the operating room;

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:00.560
and so I left on my own volition.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.623
Started medical school, and here I am now.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:05.730
- [Narrator] Since head
injuries are common

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:08.070
on the football field,
Myron works to impress

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:11.470
the importance of avoiding
concussions on young players.

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:14.683
But for Myron, his days of
tackling are behind him.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:18.670
- Football was great for
that season of my life,

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:19.800
but now this is it.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:20.740
This is the pinnacle.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:23.680
This is where I belong,
and I've told my parents

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:25.040
several times over and over again.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.117
They ask me, "Myron, how do you feel

00:02:26.117 --> 00:02:26.950
"what you're doin' now?

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:27.783
"How do you feel?"

00:02:27.783 --> 00:02:29.307
I said, "Mommy and Daddy, I feel like this

00:02:29.307 --> 00:02:30.322
"is where I belong."

00:02:30.322 --> 00:02:32.660
- [Patient] So, did you say
you played a sport before?

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:34.163
- [Myron] Yes, I played football.

00:02:34.163 --> 00:02:37.246
(soft ambient music)

